WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:10.140
I have always loved the far North and I have often let my mind wander around up there.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:17.120
I have flown above the inland ice for hours and looked down upon the ice landscape, which I thought to be permanent.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.800
We’re talking about permafrost because the Arctic perhaps is a place on Earth

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.120
where it is a common perception that time stands still.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.020
And where one can also locate the past – you can drill trough the ice, find ice cores,

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.320
and find examples of how life was a long time ago.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.740
I have of course read about sliding glaciers.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:39.860
I have seen the photos that show how a glacier has moved during the last 200 years.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.580
Civilizations have always emerged by the waterfronts, for instance in the Middle East by the rivers.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.500
What is unbelievable today is that everything is moving so fast,

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.940
that we now stand before great changes regarding the Arctic.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:59.260
The Arctic challenges our reasoning power, our fantasy, in a number of ways.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:10.400
The present threat, by all accounts, is the great tide, a flood, which once again makes water crucial to all of us.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.240
It is not perceived as a catastrophe; We are not sailing towards an iceberg like Titanic.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.140
No, the entire Earth has become the Titanic,

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:24.340
which is threatened not by water as solid liquid – ice – but rather in the liquid state which is so imperceptible.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.020
It comes so imperceptibly that at some point the Arctic will come to us as well.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.380
Actually, the Arctic is already here.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:35.360
When the highways begin to crackle, when the ground water rises it is because the Arctic has arrived to the wealthier areas.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:41.000
It is not part of our daily consciousness, also because we don’t live in what we perceive as threatened areas.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.540
We talk about climate refugees, and by that we mean people who escape dessert areas.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:51.400
But there will be a time where the Dutch, the Danes, and the Britons will have to escape from the rising oceans.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:56.980
This is what the Arctic has become to me; a metaphor for dramatic change,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.380
whereas it used to be an image of something entirely static.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.640
I have read about polar expeditions, I have read many books about it,

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:12.740
and I have always hoped that the Arctic could stay a sacred space for me; a place for fairy tales.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:16.700
Today, I can only think of it as a future nightmare.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.960
Nevertheless, I cannot be sure. Nobody can.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.680
The worst thing is that even in our time climate change deniers, now also in The White House,

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.980
still have so much power.

